  "body": "## Result\n\nThis package gives a scoped exact census for six read-only sources using thirteen singleton calls and one atomic `TRIO_{j,k,l}` connector call. Across all canonical 13-step words whose 16 total source-map applications restore every source at even multiplicity at least two, the maximum number of nonzero masks obtainable with paired readouts is 61/63. The search covers both possible source-map profiles, `(2,2,2,2,4,4)` and `(2,2,2,2,2,6)`, and allows repeated prefix states.\n\nA maximum path repairs its two missing masks with four readouts each. The completed bill is 14 source calls plus 130 output readouts, 144 root calls total. The incumbent uses 16 singleton source calls plus 126 output readouts, 142 total. The source-map profile is unchanged. For uniform source-call frame/dispatch price `f`, output-readout price `g`, and all incremental TRIO costs `rho`, the cost difference is `-2*f + 4*g + rho`; at unit prices the candidate costs `2 + rho` more. No kappa or supplier improvement is claimed.\n\n## Exact evidence\n\n- The Python census enumerates 9,321,312 complete six-label restricted-growth words; 2,342,340 match the restored source-map profiles. The full histogram and fixed-width record digest are in `CERTIFICATE.json`.\n- An independent C++ implementation recomputes pairwise prefix XORs directly and agrees on the profile count, maximum (61), maximizers (88), and complete histogram.\n- Positive control: the pinned incumbent 16-singleton word covers all 63 nonzero masks.\n- Negative controls: an invalid multiplicity profile and an out-of-alphabet label are rejected.\n\nReproduce from the repository root:\n\n```sh\npython3 -B research/six-source-trio-path-seed87a169/verify.py\ng++ -O3 -std=c++17 research/six-source-trio-path-seed87a169/independent.cpp -o /tmp/six-trio-independent\n/tmp/six-trio-independent\npython3 scripts/research_package.py --package research/six-source-trio-path-seed87a169 --check-only\n```\n\nExpected Python line: `PASS_SINGLE_TRIO_CENSUS eligible=2342340 max=61/63 at_max=88 completed_queries=144 incumbent=142`.\n\n## Scope and overlap\n\nBase commit: `0fdd7d82de03e43c9e5a1000dfbcd380d1b687d2`. Selected-record SHA-256: `10b9e340fd8e354a37a0c4813c90e5de1dd42044b5f6aca4a3fc5a42b685fa32`. Pinned inputs and source blobs are listed in `SOURCES.json`.\n\nThe reviewed domain of [PR #1518](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1518) is a ten-call, one-TRIO, twelve-map census. This result covers fourteen source calls and sixteen map applications. [Discussion #1504](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/discussions/1504) concerns three and five sources. The fresh overlap snapshot also included [PR #2128](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/2128), which reaches `(k,W)=(14,16)` with six-source DUO calls; the call family and construction are different. The bounded negative here gives a direct six-source cost comparison for a TRIO at the same `(k,W)` frontier.\n\nThis conclusion applies only to one TRIO, thirteen singleton calls, the two restored 16-map profiles, and the paired-readout connector model. It does not exclude longer paths, multiple TRIO calls, other alphabets, changed restoration rules, or different tariffs. The selected frontier is unchanged.\n\n## Credit\n\nPrepared by OpenAI Codex with substantial AI assistance in search design, implementation, independent cross-checking, cost accounting, and writing. No predecessor implementation is copied; predecessor scope and source attribution are retained in the package.\n",
